  "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B001",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "for the invention and development of optical lattice clocks"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B004",
    "B020"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B001 remains the most complete experimental case: the magic-wavelength principle made it possible to confine many atoms while preserving an exceptionally narrow clock transition, and the resulting clocks have been independently reproduced at outstanding accuracy and used for mature precision comparisons and fundamental measurements. The achievement is a distinct physical method, not simply a performance increment in timekeeping. Katori's foundational proposal and Ye's decisive experimental development remain a compact and complementary attribution, provided the prize is drawn narrowly around optical lattice clocks.",
    "case_against": "The central reservation remains historical attribution. Optical-frequency metrology, optical clocks, and later lattice-clock performance advances have a long and collective lineage. A final historical review must verify that Katori and Ye alone fairly delimit the invention and defining development of the magic-wavelength lattice clock, and the citation should not imply credit for all optical-clock metrology or for a future redefinition of the second.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "danielsson-ulf",
        "point": "Danielsson favors B012 because inflation and primordial perturbation theory organize decades of cosmological observations, while acknowledging the lack of a distinctive direct signature and of an agreed microscopic realization.",
        "response": "I accept the depth and observational reach of B012, and its indirect support is far stronger than a speculative proposal. Nevertheless, the absence of a discriminating direct signature leaves a real ambiguity about what precisely has been established. B001 offers a directly measurable, independently repeatable physical advance whose operational principle and consequences can be sharply tested in many laboratories."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "eriksson-olle",
        "point": "Eriksson favors B005 as a clear theory-to-experiment discovery of the quantum spin Hall effect, while reserving judgment about the breadth of its experimental and materials attribution.",
        "response": "The theory-to-experiment chain in B005 is indeed compelling, and its identification of a new topological state is prize-worthy physics. I give B001 precedence because its two-person attribution is presently more tractable and its measurement principle is directly isolated from the later engineering achievements. B005 still requires a demanding inquiry into whether Molenkamp fairly represents the experimental discovery and how the citation can avoid absorbing the wider topological-materials field."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson argues that B001 is preferable to circuit QED because lattice clocks have a sharply delimited physical principle, broad independent reproduction, and mature fundamental-measurement uses.",
        "response": "I agree with this comparison. Circuit QED is an extraordinary experimental platform, but its foundational result remains difficult to disentangle from the wider and still rapidly developing superconducting-quantum-computing programme. The remaining issue for B001 is not experimental maturity but a precise historical boundary; that can be addressed by retaining the narrow lattice-clock citation."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether historical priority and contribution records support limiting an optical-lattice-clock prize to Katori and Ye.",
      "How narrowly the citation must be framed to distinguish the magic-wavelength lattice-clock breakthrough from earlier optical metrology and subsequent performance advances.",
      "Whether the absence of a distinctive direct signature should ultimately prevent recognition of B012 despite its extensive indirect observational support."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "No direct conflict or collaboration requiring recusal is apparent from the supplied profile. My WACQT leadership overlaps institutionally with Göran Johansson's Chalmers environment, but no specific connection to B001 or its proposed laureates is identified."
  }
}
